<%# AIDEV-NOTE: Revisit this page when: student logins ship, AI features launch (name providers), Cove forms an LLC (update operating party), analytics is added, or any new data processor is added. %>
<section>
  <h2>Scope</h2>
  <p>This policy explains what information <%= Jumpstart.config.business_name %> collects, how we use it, and the choices you have. Cove is for families in the United States, and this policy applies to everyone who uses Cove.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account information:</strong> your name, email address, and account settings.</li>
    <li><strong>Google sign-in data:</strong> if you sign in with Google, your name, email address, and profile photo (see Google user data below).</li>
    <li><strong>Family members and invitations:</strong> the other parent you invite to your family, and the invitations you send.</li>
    <li><strong>Student information:</strong> the information you enter about your students.</li>
    <li><strong>Billing information:</strong> Stripe holds your payment card number. We keep only the card brand and last four digits, along with your plan and billing history.</li>
    <li><strong>Support messages:</strong> anything you send us when you ask for help.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> IP address, browser type, and server logs.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Children's information</h2>
  <p><strong>Children do not have Cove accounts.</strong> Parents create and control everything about their students. We collect information about children only from their parents.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Information about your children is never sold and never used for advertising.</li>
    <li>It is never used to train AI models.</li>
    <li>You can view, edit, or delete your students' information at any time.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Before student logins launch, we will update this policy. Any student login will be created and controlled by a parent.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <p>We use your information to provide, maintain, and secure Cove; to communicate with you about your account; to process payments; to respond to support requests; and to improve Cove.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>AI features</h2>
  <p>AI features in Cove, if we offer them, are optional. AI providers receive only the information a feature needs to work. We will use only providers whose contracts forbid training on your data. We will name those providers here when AI features launch.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Google user data</h2>
  <p>When you sign in with Google, Cove receives your name, email address, and profile photo from Google. We use them only to identify you, sign you in, and operate your Cove account. We do not use Google user data for advertising, and we do not sell it. We store a sanitized record of the sign-in response to support your connected account.</p>
  <p>Cove's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs complies with the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Who we share information with</h2>
  <p>We share information only with the service providers that help us run Cove, and only as needed for them to do their work:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Stripe</strong> processes payments.</li>
    <li><strong>Loops</strong> sends our emails. Loops sends all of our account and billing emails, and marketing emails if you opt in.</li>
    <li><strong>Honeybadger</strong> helps us detect and fix errors.</li>
    <li><strong>Render</strong> hosts Cove.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We may also disclose information when the law requires it, or as part of a merger, sale, or transfer of Cove's business, in which case this policy continues to apply to your information.</p>
  <p><strong>Your information is never sold or shared for targeted advertising.</strong></p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>Cove uses only essential cookies, which keep you signed in and keep your account secure. We do not use analytics or advertising trackers.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
  <p>We keep your information while your account is active and as long as needed to provide Cove, meet legal obligations, resolve disputes, and enforce our agreements. You can delete your students' information at any time, and you can ask us to delete your account and personal information. We may keep limited billing records where the law requires it.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational safeguards to protect your information. No internet service can guarantee absolute security.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask to access, correct, or delete your information, and you can opt out of marketing email at any time using the link in any email or in your preferences. We honor these requests for all users in the United States, regardless of state. To make a request, contact us below.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If we change this policy, we will update the date at the top of this page. For material changes, we will tell you before they take effect.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Contact us</h2>
  <p>Questions or requests about your privacy? Email <a href="mailto:<%= Jumpstart.config.support_email %>"><%= Jumpstart.config.support_email %></a>.</p>
</section>
